@tradition float-hour
// W3 rec deck words. Wednesdays 21:30-22:15 from Day 3, the float room; Matthias Oduya dims the orbs, quiet music, no talking. Tap to float: rest, mood.
== mail
- Float hour tomorrow, {time} in the float room. Matthias dims the orbs, someone plays something quiet, and nobody talks. Come and drift.
== ask
- Float hour tonight. No talking. You'll love it.   #warm
- Coming to float hour? You sleep like a baby after. A tired, floaty baby.   #funny
== here
- Shh.   #warm
- Just drift.   #warm
== thanks
- You step into a fifth of a g as the orbs dim. Nobody says a word. You drift, and the day goes quiet.   #warm
== chatter
- I slept so well after float hour. Best sleep all week.   #warm
- Someone hummed at float hour. Matthias gave them a look. A kind look, but a look.   #funny
- Float hour's the quietest place on the ship.
